    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Navigating a roof insurance claim in Utah requires a clear step-by-step process and careful handling of your insurance company."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "The 6-Step Claim Process"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Inspection: Have a local roofer inspect your roof before you call the insurance company. They will take photos and document whether the damage meets the threshold for a claim."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review Your Policy: Check your deductible amount and whether your policy pays out on a Replacement Cost Value (RCV) or Actual Cash Value (ACV) basis."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File the Claim: Contact your insurance provider with the date of the storm or loss and a clear description of the damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the Adjuster: Ask your roofing contractor to be on your roof alongside the insurance adjuster to ensure no storm damage is missed."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review the Scope of Work: The insurance company will send an estimate breakdown (the scope). Your contractor can help verify if it covers the necessary repairs or if a supplement is needed."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Complete the Build and Release Depreciation: Once the work is done, your roofer sends a final invoice so the insurance company releases the remaining withheld depreciation funds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Tips for Utah Homeowners"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Watch out for your claims history: Opinions on Reddit are mixed regarding door-to-door roofers; while some have good experiences, users warn against letting a roofing company file a claim on your behalf or sign over full representation without reading the fine print.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Reddit",
                "link": "https://www.reddit.com/r/Utah/comments/1jk2w05/roofer_wants_to_file_a_claim_in_our_behalf_to_our/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Know your coverage: Standard Utah policies cover wind, hail, and falling trees, but generally exclude flood or neglect."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "State assistance: If you run into a major dispute or unfair denial with your provider, you can contact the Utah Insurance Department consumer division at 801-957-9305.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
                "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like more specific help, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of damage occurred (hail, wind, snow/ice)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Have you already contacted your insurance company?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more tailored advice for your situation."
      },
